.TH BOOK 1
.SH NAME
book, book2tex, mkindex \- make a book
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B book
[
.B -f
] [
.BI -p " works.bib"
] [
.BI -S " style"
] [
.BI -o " book.pdf"
]
.I book.ms
.br
.B book2tex
[
.BI -p " works.bib"
] [
.BI -o " book.tex"
] [
.I book.ms
]
.br
.B mkindex
[
.B -l
] [
.I book.out ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Book
makes a PDF of a book written with
.BR -mbook ,
the macros of
.IR troff (6).
It runs
.IR refer (1)
with the database
.I works.bib
(its citations in the style,
.B chicago
by default),
.IR pic (1),
.IR tbl (1)
and
.IR eqn (1)
(each if the book has anything for it),
.IR troff (1)
as often as the book's table of contents, references and index need
to settle (each pass learning from the one before, through
.IR book .aux),
and
.IR tr2pdf (1).
Troff's output is kept as
.IR book .out,
for the document views.
A book with
.B .printindex
has its index made by
.I mkindex
after each pass.
.PP
A book is set as a draft unless
.B -f
is given: then as it goes to press, with microtypography (punctuation
hanging into the margins, glyphs widened or narrowed a little), as
.IR troff 's
.B .mtp
and
.B .mte
set them.
.PP
.I Book2tex
writes the book as LaTeX, for LuaLaTeX, for a publisher who wants it:
each of
.BR -mbook 's
macros as the LaTeX it stands for, the citations as biblatex-chicago's,
the equations as LaTeX's mathematics, the tables as tabulars, the
pictures (with
.BR -o )
drawn as PDFs of their own beside it.
.PP
.I Mkindex
reads troff's output for the entries
.B .index
put there and each page's folio, and writes the index
.B .printindex
sets, in the order of
.IR "The Chicago Manual of Style" .
With
.B -l
each page is a link to it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
book -p works.bib thesis.ms
book -f -p works.bib -o press.pdf thesis.ms
book2tex -p works.bib -o thesis.tex thesis.ms
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /dis/book
.br
